a-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$u^*\\in H^*$\">$u^*\\in H^*$</span> there is a unique <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$u\\in H$\">$u\\in H$</span> such that <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\langle u^*,v\\rangle =(u,v) \\qquad (v\\in H).  \\]\">\\[  \\langle u^*,v\\rangle =(u,v) \\qquad (v\\in H).  \\]</span> The map <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$u^*\\mapsto u$\">$u^*\\mapsto u$</span> is a linear isomorphism from <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$H^*$\">$H^*$</span> onto <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$H$\">$H$</span>. ","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: group"]},"previous":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixD#def:dual-pairing-reflexive-banach-space","next":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixD#def:adjoint-symmetric-operator","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixD#def:hilbert-space","title":"def:hilbert-space","label":"def:hilbert-space"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixD#def:bounded-linear-functional-dual-space","title":"def:bounded-linear-functional-dual-space","label":"def:bounded-linear-functional-dual-space"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixD#def:adjoint-symmetric-operator","title":"def:adjoint-symmetric-operator","label":"def:adjoint-symmetric-operator"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixD#thm:riesz-representation-theorem","title":"thm:riesz-representation-theorem","tex":"\\begin{theorem}[Riesz Representation Theorem]\n\\label{thm:riesz-representation-theorem}\n\\uses{def:hilbert-space, def:bounded-linear-functional-dual-space}\n\\dcref{appD:thm-2}\n\\group{Functional Analysis}\n\nFor every $u^*\\in H^*$ there is a unique $u\\in H$ such that\n\\[\n\\langle u^*,v\\rangle=(u,v)\n\\qquad(v\\in H).\n\\]\nThe map $u^*\\ma